---
/**
 * Where a practitioner lists a practice, confirms a listing, corrects it or asks for it to be removed.
 *
 * The site is static and keeps no server, and ships no script (scripts/crawl-audit.mjs refuses one). A
 * form posting to a mailto: address made browsers warn that the form was not secure, and did nothing
 * where no mail app was set up, so this page uses a prefilled mailto link instead, the same as the
 * per-listing links. Nothing is stored by this page and no third-party form service sees it.
 *
 * Nothing submitted is published as it arrives. A new listing is checked the same way a collected one
 * is: the registration number against the state or national register, and the practice name, address
 * and phone against the practice's own published details or a call to that number. Only then does it go
 * through the same admission script as everything else.
 */
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { rel } from '../../lib/site';
import { emailLinks } from '../../lib/email-links';
const TO = 'contact@ageayurveda.com';
const BODY = [
  'What would you like to do? (add my practice / confirm my listing / correct my listing / remove my listing)', '',
  'Existing listing address (if any):', '',
  "Practitioner's full name:", '',
  'Qualification:', '',
  'Registration number and the council that issued it (needed for a new listing):', '',
  'Practice name:', '',
  'Full address with PIN code:', '',
  'Business phone number to publish:', '',
  'Practice website (optional):', '',
  'Anything else (services, hours, what to correct):', '',
  'I run this practice or am authorised by it, and I agree to the practitioner name, practice name, address and business phone above being published in the directory. I can ask for them to be corrected or removed at any time.',
].join('\n');
const MAIL = emailLinks(TO, 'Practitioner directory submission', BODY);
---
<Page
  title="List or verify your Ayurvedic practice"
  description="For Ayurvedic practitioners in India: add your practice to the Nighantu directory, confirm or correct an existing listing, or ask for it to be removed. Free, and checked before anything is published."
  canonical="/practitioners/submit/"
  trail={[{ label: 'Practitioners', href: '/practitioners/' }, { label: 'List or verify your practice' }]}
>
  <h1>List or verify your Ayurvedic practice</h1>
  <p class="answer">Listing is free and takes a few minutes. We publish four things about a practice: the practitioner's name, the practice's name, its address and a business phone number. We check every submission before it appears, and we never list a personal phone number.</p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Press <strong>Write to us</strong> below, or <strong>Gmail</strong> or <strong>Outlook</strong> if you use those in your browser. An email opens with a short form already in the message. Fill it in and send it. If you are already listed, the button on your listing opens an email with the listing's address filled in.</li>
    <li>We check the registration number against the state or national register, and the address and phone against your practice's own published details, or by calling the business number.</li>
    <li>Once checked, the listing goes live, usually within a week, showing the date it was checked. A verified registration is shown on the listing.</li>
  </ol>

  <p><a class="practitioner-cta" href={MAIL.mailto}>Write to us</a> <a class="practitioner-cta" href={MAIL.gmail} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gmail</a> <a class="practitioner-cta" href={MAIL.outlook} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Outlook</a></p>
  <p class="hint">"Write to us" uses the email program on your computer. If nothing opens (common on Windows), use the Gmail or Outlook button. Otherwise, email <a href={`mailto:${TO}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Practitioner directory')}`}>{TO}</a> with: what you would like to do, the practitioner's name, qualification, registration number and council, practice name, full address with PIN, business phone, and your agreement to those details being published.</p>

  <p>Prefer to write directly? Email <a href={`mailto:${TO}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Practitioner directory')}`}>{TO}</a>. You can also ask for a listing to be removed without giving a reason, and we will remove it.</p>

  <h2>What we do with your details</h2>
  <p>We use what you send only to check and publish your listing. Your email address and anything you mark as not for publication are never published. Testimonials are not taken through this form; where your practice publishes them on its own website, the listing may quote short excerpts with a link. <a href={rel('/practitioners/about/')}>How the directory is made</a>.</p>

</Page>
